###
post: Layered graph layout
agent: claude

`layered(g)` places the nodes of a directed graph in layers, the way
Graphviz's `dot` does (Sugiyama, Tagawa and Toda, 1981; Gansner, Koutsofios,
North and Vo, 1993), and routes every edge between them. The input is a
`LayoutInput`: each node's size, each edge's ends, and for each edge whether
it runs against the direction of the layers (a value carried to the next
pass of a loop), how much it wants to be straight, where it leaves its
source and enters its target, and the size of its label. The output is a
`Layered`: each node's center, each edge's route as a polyline, and each
label's center.

Layers run down the page (the rank axis is y, growing downward); a caller
that wants them left to right swaps the sizes on the way in and the
coordinates on the way out. The four phases:

1. **Cycles.** A depth-first search from each node in order turns every edge
   that closes a cycle around; so does every edge the caller marks `back`.
   The rest of the layout sees a graph with no cycles.
2. **Ranks.** Longest path: a node's rank is one more than the largest rank
   of the nodes with an edge into it. A node with no edge in is then moved
   down to one rank above the nearest node it points to, so it is not left at
   the top, far from what it feeds.
3. **Order.** An edge that spans several ranks gets a dummy node on each rank
   between, so every edge joins adjacent ranks. The nodes of each rank are
   ordered by barycenter sweeps, down then up, twelve in all: each node goes
   to the mean position of its neighbors on the rank before. The order with
   the fewest crossings is kept; then two neighbors on a rank change places
   while that removes crossings (the transpose step).
4. **Coordinates.** Each node wants to sit at the weighted mean of its
   neighbors' positions (an edge's weight is larger between dummies, so a long
   edge runs straight). On each rank the positions nearest those wishes that
   keep the order and the gaps are found exactly, by pool-adjacent-violators
   (a least-squares fit under ordering constraints). Sweeps alternate down and
   up.

The output is deterministic: no hash, no random choice, ties broken by node
index.

Used with `import graphlayout`.
###

#| What `layered` needs: node sizes and edges.
#: w          each node's size across the rank axis (its width)
#: h          each node's size along the rank axis (its height)
#: efrom      each edge's source node
#: eto        each edge's target node
#: eback      1 when the edge is drawn against the ranks (the target comes first)
#: eweight    how much the edge wants to be straight, 1 by default
#: elen       the least number of ranks the edge spans, 1 by default
#: sport      where the edge leaves its source: an offset from the source's center, across
#: tport      where it enters its target, the same way
#: label_w    the size of the edge's label (0 for none)
#: label_h    its height
#: node_gap   the least space between two nodes of a rank
#: rank_gap   the space between two ranks
#: hint       where each node was across in an earlier layout (its center), when `hinted` is 1
#: hinted     1 for a node that should stay where it was: its order in its rank
#:            against the other hinted nodes is kept, and it sits at its hint
#:            unless the gaps push it
#: sides      1 when an edge may leave or enter a node from its side (toward a
#:            lane beside it); 0 for always from the node's foot to the next
#:            node's head
record LayoutInput {
    w: Arr
    h: Arr
    efrom: Arr
    eto: Arr
    eback: Arr
    eweight: Arr
    elen: Arr
    sport: Arr
    tport: Arr
    label_w: Arr
    label_h: Arr
    node_gap: Num
    rank_gap: Num
    hint: Arr
    hinted: Arr
    sides: Num
}

#| Where `layered` put the nodes and the edges.
#: x          each node's center across
#: y          each node's center along the ranks (down)
#: rank       each node's rank
#: order      each node's place in its rank
#: reversed   1 for an edge the layout turned around (its route still runs from its source to its target)
#: route_start where each edge's route begins in route_x, route_y; one more entry than edges
#: label_x    the center of each edge's label
#: label_y    the same, along the ranks
#: width      the extent of the drawing across
#: height     its extent along the ranks
#: crossings  the number of edge crossings between adjacent ranks
record Layered {
    x: Arr
    y: Arr
    rank: Arr
    order: Arr
    reversed: Arr
    route_start: Arr
    route_x: Arr
    route_y: Arr
    label_x: Arr
    label_y: Arr
    width: Num
    height: Num
    crossings: Num
}

#| Order sweeps: alternately down and up.
SWEEPS = 12
#| Coordinate sweeps: alternately down and up.
PLACE_SWEEPS = 24
#| The most passes of the transpose step over the ranks.
TRANSPOSE_ROUNDS = 8
#| The width of a dummy node: an edge passing through a rank.
DUMMY_W = 6
#| The weight of an edge's piece between a real node and a dummy, and between
#| two dummies: a long edge bends at its ends and runs straight between.
REAL_DUMMY_WEIGHT = 0.1
DUMMY_DUMMY_WEIGHT = 8
#| How far a port can shift a node's barycenter, as a fraction of a place.
PORT_PULL = 0.45
#| How much more a real node's wish counts than a dummy's, when the two
#| cannot both be met (Sugiyama's priority method gives dummies the higher
#| priority, to keep long edges straight; here the boxes stay aligned and the
#| edge bends around them).
REAL_PRIORITY = 20
#| The weight that keeps a node with no neighbors where it was.
STAY_WEIGHT = 0.05
#| The least sideways step a long edge's route takes between two ranks;
#| smaller ones are straightened.
KINK = 4
#| With hints: the least step between the order keys of two hinted nodes.
HINT_ORDER_EPS = 1e-6
#| How far a self-loop reaches out from its node.
SELF_LOOP_REACH = 16
#| The gap between an edge and its label, when the label sits beside it.
LABEL_PAD = 4

#| An input with every edge plain: straight wishes of weight 1, centered
#| ports, no labels, no hints.
def layout_input(w: Arr, h: Arr, efrom: Arr, eto: Arr, node_gap, rank_gap) -> LayoutInput {
    ne = len(efrom)
    n = len(w)
    return LayoutInput { w: w, h: h, efrom: efrom, eto: eto, eback: zeros(ne), eweight: zeros(ne) + 1, elen: zeros(ne) + 1, sport: zeros(ne), tport: zeros(ne), label_w: zeros(ne), label_h: zeros(ne), node_gap: node_gap, rank_gap: rank_gap, hint: zeros(n), hinted: zeros(n), sides: 1 }
}

#| The indices 0 .. len(keys) - 1 grouped by key (keys are 0 .. n - 1), in
#| order within a group: `items[start[k]] .. items[start[k + 1] - 1]` are
#| the indices with key k.
def group_by(n, keys: Arr) {
    start = zeros(n + 1)
    for k to len(keys) {
        start[keys[k] + 1] += 1
    }
    for v to n {
        start[v + 1] += start[v]
    }
    next = zeros(n)
    for v to n {
        next[v] = start[v]
    }
    items = zeros(len(keys))
    for k to len(keys) {
        items[next[keys[k]]] = k
        next[keys[k]] += 1
    }
    return start, items
}

#| Sort `items[lo:hi]` by `key[item]`, keeping the order of equal keys.
def sort_part(items: Arr, lo, hi, key: Arr) {
    part = items[lo:hi]
    items[lo:hi] = take(part, argsort(take(key, part)))
}

#| Which edges close a cycle: a depth-first search from each node in index
#| order, following the edges not already marked `back`. 1 for an edge the
#| layout turns around.
def cycle_edges(n, efrom: Arr, eto: Arr, eback: Arr) -> Arr {
    ne = len(efrom)
    rev = zeros(ne)
    for e to ne {
        if eback[e] == 1 and efrom[e] != eto[e] {
            rev[e] = 1
        }
    }
    ostart, oedges = group_by(n, efrom)
    # 0 not seen, 1 on the path, 2 finished
    state = zeros(n)
    stack = zeros(n)
    cursor = zeros(n)
    for root to n {
        if state[root] != 0 {
            continue
        }
        top = 0
        stack[0] = root
        state[root] = 1
        cursor[root] = ostart[root]
        while top >= 0 {
            u = stack[top]
            if cursor[u] == ostart[u + 1] {
                state[u] = 2
                top -= 1
                continue
            }
            e = oedges[cursor[u]]
            cursor[u] += 1
            v = eto[e]
            if eback[e] == 1 or v == u {
                continue
            }
            if state[v] == 1 {
                rev[e] = 1
            }
            else if state[v] == 0 {
                top += 1
                stack[top] = v
                state[v] = 1
                cursor[v] = ostart[v]
            }
        }
    }
    return rev
}

#| Longest-path ranks of the graph with edges `a -> b`, each spanning at
#| least `elen` ranks (no cycles; self loops are skipped), then each node
#| with no edge in moved down as near as it may go to the nearest node it
#| points to.
def longest_path_ranks(n, a: Arr, b: Arr, elen: Arr) -> Arr {
    ne = len(a)
    indeg = zeros(n)
    for e to ne {
        if a[e] != b[e] {
            indeg[b[e]] += 1
        }
    }
    ostart, oedges = group_by(n, a)
    rank = zeros(n)
    # Kahn's order: a queue of the nodes whose edges in are all counted
    queue = zeros(n)
    head = 0
    tail = 0
    for v to n {
        if indeg[v] == 0 {
            queue[tail] = v
            tail += 1
        }
    }
    left = copy(indeg)
    while head < tail {
        u = queue[head]
        head += 1
        for k from ostart[u] to ostart[u + 1] {
            e = oedges[k]
            v = b[e]
            if v == u {
                continue
            }
            rank[v] = max(rank[v], rank[u] + elen[e])
            left[v] -= 1
            if left[v] == 0 {
                queue[tail] = v
                tail += 1
            }
        }
    }
    # sources, latest first: down to one rank above the nearest successor
    for k from tail - 1 to -1 by -1 {
        u = queue[k]
        if indeg[u] != 0 or ostart[u + 1] == ostart[u] {
            continue
        }
        nearest = -1
        for j from ostart[u] to ostart[u + 1] {
            e = oedges[j]
            v = b[e]
            if v != u and (nearest < 0 or rank[v] - elen[e] < nearest) {
                nearest = rank[v] - elen[e]
            }
        }
        if nearest > 0 {
            rank[u] = nearest
        }
    }
    return rank
}

#| The crossings between rank r and rank r + 1: pairs of pieces whose ends
#| are in opposite order. `pieces` lists the pieces from rank r.
def crossings_between(pieces: Arr, lo, hi, psrc: Arr, pdst: Arr, pos: Arr) {
    c = 0
    for i from lo to hi {
        for j from i + 1 to hi {
            p = pieces[i]
            q = pieces[j]
            d1 = pos[psrc[p]] - pos[psrc[q]]
            d2 = pos[pdst[p]] - pos[pdst[q]]
            if d1 * d2 < 0 {
                c += 1
            }
        }
    }
    return c
}

#| The crossings between the pieces at `v` and those at `w` when `v` is left
#| of `w` on their rank: with the rank before (pieces in) and after (pieces out).
def pair_crossings(v, w, instart: Arr, initems: Arr, psrc: Arr, outstart: Arr, outitems: Arr, pdst: Arr, pos: Arr) {
    c = 0
    for a from instart[v] to instart[v + 1] {
        for b from instart[w] to instart[w + 1] {
            if pos[psrc[initems[a]]] > pos[psrc[initems[b]]] {
                c += 1
            }
        }
    }
    for a from outstart[v] to outstart[v + 1] {
        for b from outstart[w] to outstart[w + 1] {
            if pos[pdst[outitems[a]]] > pos[pdst[outitems[b]]] {
                c += 1
            }
        }
    }
    return c
}

#| All crossings of an order.
def count_crossings(nranks, pstart: Arr, pitems: Arr, psrc: Arr, pdst: Arr, pos: Arr) {
    c = 0
    for r to nranks {
        c += crossings_between(pitems, pstart[r], pstart[r + 1], psrc, pdst, pos)
    }
    return c
}

#| The positions nearest `t` (weights `wt`) that keep the order of `nodes`
#| and at least `sep[i]` between node i and node i + 1: pool adjacent
#| violators on t - (the running sum of the gaps). Writes into `x`.
def place_rank(nodes: Arr, lo, hi, t: Arr, wt: Arr, sep: Arr, x: Arr) {
    m = hi - lo
    if m == 0 {
        return 0
    }
    offset = zeros(m)
    for i from 1 to m {
        offset[i] = offset[i - 1] + sep[nodes[lo + i - 1]]
    }
    # blocks: their mean, weight, and first member
    bmean = zeros(m)
    bweight = zeros(m)
    bfirst = zeros(m)
    nb = 0
    for i to m {
        v = nodes[lo + i]
        bmean[nb] = t[v] - offset[i]
        bweight[nb] = wt[v]
        bfirst[nb] = i
        nb += 1
        while nb > 1 and bmean[nb - 2] > bmean[nb - 1] {
            wsum = bweight[nb - 2] + bweight[nb - 1]
            bmean[nb - 2] = (bmean[nb - 2] * bweight[nb - 2] + bmean[nb - 1] * bweight[nb - 1]) / wsum
            bweight[nb - 2] = wsum
            nb -= 1
        }
    }
    for k to nb {
        last = m
        if k + 1 < nb {
            last = bfirst[k + 1]
        }
        for i from bfirst[k] to last {
            x[nodes[lo + i]] = bmean[k] + offset[i]
        }
    }
    return 0
}

#| The weighted median of `vals`: the value where half the weight is on
#| each side; midway between two values when the halves meet between them.
#| (Graphviz places a node by minimizing the weighted sum of |x_u - x_v|, whose
#| optimum is this median: a heavy edge wins outright, where a mean would
#| bend it toward every light one.)
def weighted_median(vals: Arr, wts: Arr) {
    m = len(vals)
    order = zeros(m)
    for i to m {
        order[i] = i
    }
    sort_part(order, 0, m, vals)
    half = sum(wts) / 2
    acc = 0
    for i to m {
        acc += wts[order[i]]
        if abs(acc - half) <= 1e-12 * half and i + 1 < m {
            return (vals[order[i]] + vals[order[i + 1]]) / 2
        }
        if acc > half {
            return vals[order[i]]
        }
    }
    return vals[order[m - 1]]
}

#| The elements of `v` in the opposite order.
def reversed_copy(v: Arr) -> Arr {
    m = len(v)
    out = zeros(m)
    for i to m {
        out[i] = v[m - 1 - i]
    }
    return out
}

#| Whether no node of `v`'s rank but `v` lies between `v`'s center and `lane`
#| (nodes are 0 .. n - 1; the rest are dummies): an edge can then leave `v`
#| from its side toward the lane.
def clear_beside(v, lane, n, rank: Arr, x: Arr, nw: Arr) {
    lo = min(x[v], lane)
    hi = max(x[v], lane)
    for u to n {
        if u != v and rank[u] == rank[v] and x[u] + nw[u] / 2 > lo and x[u] - nw[u] / 2 < hi {
            return false
        }
    }
    return true
}

#| Lay out the graph (see the module's text).
def layered(inp: LayoutInput) -> Layered {
    n = len(inp.w)
    ne = len(inp.efrom)
    rev = cycle_edges(n, inp.efrom, inp.eto, inp.eback)
    # each edge as the layout sees it: from a to b, a on an earlier rank
    a = zeros(ne)
    b = zeros(ne)
    for e to ne {
        a[e] = inp.efrom[e]
        b[e] = inp.eto[e]
        if rev[e] == 1 {
            a[e] = inp.eto[e]
            b[e] = inp.efrom[e]
        }
    }
    rank0 = longest_path_ranks(n, a, b, inp.elen)

    # ---- dummies: every edge becomes pieces between adjacent ranks
    nw = copy(inp.w)
    nh = copy(inp.h)
    rank = copy(rank0)
    psrc = []
    pdst = []
    pedge = []
    pweight = []
    psoff = []
    ptoff = []
    # per edge: its first piece, its piece count, the dummy that holds its label
    efirst = zeros(ne)
    ecount = zeros(ne)
    elabel = zeros(ne) - 1
    # each dummy's lane: where its edge passes, from its center
    doff = []
    total = n
    for e to ne {
        efirst[e] = len(psrc)
        if a[e] == b[e] {
            continue
        }
        span = rank[b[e]] - rank[a[e]]
        # the ports: an edge turned around leaves from its target's port
        sp = inp.sport[e]
        tp = inp.tport[e]
        if rev[e] == 1 {
            sp = inp.tport[e]
            tp = inp.sport[e]
        }
        prev = a[e]
        mid = floor((span - 1) / 2)
        for k from 1 to span {
            d = total
            total += 1
            dw = DUMMY_W
            dh = 0
            # the dummy that holds the label is as wide as the label and a
            # gap; the edge runs down its left side
            lane = 0
            if k - 1 == mid and inp.label_w[e] > 0 {
                dw = inp.label_w[e] + 2 * LABEL_PAD
                dh = inp.label_h[e]
                lane = -dw / 2
                elabel[e] = d
            }
            doff = append(doff, lane)
            nw = append(nw, dw)
            nh = append(nh, dh)
            rank = append(rank, rank[a[e]] + k)
            psrc = append(psrc, prev)
            pdst = append(pdst, d)
            pedge = append(pedge, e)
            pw = REAL_DUMMY_WEIGHT
            if k > 1 {
                pw = DUMMY_DUMMY_WEIGHT
            }
            pweight = append(pweight, pw * inp.eweight[e])
            if k == 1 {
                psoff = append(psoff, sp)
            }
            else {
                psoff = append(psoff, doff[prev - n])
            }
            ptoff = append(ptoff, lane)
            prev = d
        }
        psrc = append(psrc, prev)
        pdst = append(pdst, b[e])
        pedge = append(pedge, e)
        pw = 1
        if span > 1 {
            pw = REAL_DUMMY_WEIGHT
        }
        pweight = append(pweight, pw * inp.eweight[e])
        if span == 1 {
            psoff = append(psoff, sp)
        }
        else {
            psoff = append(psoff, doff[prev - n])
        }
        ptoff = append(ptoff, tp)
        ecount[e] = len(psrc) - efirst[e]
    }
    np = len(psrc)
    nranks = 0
    for v to total {
        nranks = max(nranks, rank[v] + 1)
    }

    # ---- order within each rank
    lstart, lnodes = group_by(nranks, rank)
    pos = zeros(total)
    for r to nranks {
        for i from lstart[r] to lstart[r + 1] {
            pos[lnodes[i]] = i - lstart[r]
        }
    }
    prank = zeros(np)
    for p to np {
        prank[p] = rank[psrc[p]]
    }
    pstart, pitems = group_by(nranks, prank)
    instart, initems = group_by(total, pdst)
    outstart, outitems = group_by(total, psrc)
    # with hints, the first order is the earlier layout's, and each new node
    # goes where its neighbors put it
    hinting = sum(inp.hinted) > 0
    if hinting {
        est = zeros(total)
        known = zeros(total)
        for v to n {
            if inp.hinted[v] == 1 {
                est[v] = inp.hint[v]
                known[v] = 1
            }
        }
        for pass to 2 {
            for step to nranks {
                r = step
                if pass == 1 {
                    r = nranks - 1 - step
                }
                for i from lstart[r] to lstart[r + 1] {
                    v = lnodes[i]
                    if known[v] == 1 {
                        continue
                    }
                    s = 0
                    c = 0
                    if pass == 0 {
                        for k from instart[v] to instart[v + 1] {
                            p = initems[k]
                            if known[psrc[p]] == 1 {
                                s += est[psrc[p]] + psoff[p] - ptoff[p]
                                c += 1
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    else {
                        for k from outstart[v] to outstart[v + 1] {
                            p = outitems[k]
                            if known[pdst[p]] == 1 {
                                s += est[pdst[p]] + ptoff[p] - psoff[p]
                                c += 1
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    if c > 0 {
                        est[v] = s / c
                        known[v] = 1
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        # a node nothing placed goes after the rest of its rank, in its order
        far_right = 0
        for v to total {
            if known[v] == 1 {
                far_right = max(far_right, est[v])
            }
        }
        for v to total {
            if known[v] == 0 {
                est[v] = far_right + 1 + pos[v]
            }
        }
        for r to nranks {
            sort_part(lnodes, lstart[r], lstart[r + 1], est)
            for i from lstart[r] to lstart[r + 1] {
                pos[lnodes[i]] = i - lstart[r]
            }
        }
    }
    best = count_crossings(nranks, pstart, pitems, psrc, pdst, pos)
    bestpos = copy(pos)
    key = zeros(total)
    for sweep to SWEEPS {
        down = mod(sweep, 2) == 0
        for step from 1 to nranks {
            r = step
            if not down {
                r = nranks - 1 - step
            }
            for i from lstart[r] to lstart[r + 1] {
                v = lnodes[i]
                s = 0
                c = 0
                if down {
                    for k from instart[v] to instart[v + 1] {
                        p = initems[k]
                        u = psrc[p]
                        s += pos[u] + min(PORT_PULL, max(-PORT_PULL, psoff[p] / max(nw[u], 1)))
                        c += 1
                    }
                }
                else {
                    for k from outstart[v] to outstart[v + 1] {
                        p = outitems[k]
                        u = pdst[p]
                        s += pos[u] + min(PORT_PULL, max(-PORT_PULL, ptoff[p] / max(nw[u], 1)))
                        c += 1
                    }
                }
                if c > 0 {
                    key[v] = s / c
                }
                else {
                    key[v] = pos[v]
                }
            }
            # hinted nodes keep their order among themselves
            if hinting {
                last = -1
                for i from lstart[r] to lstart[r + 1] {
                    v = lnodes[i]
                    if v < n and inp.hinted[v] == 1 {
                        if last >= 0 and key[v] <= key[last] {
                            key[v] = key[last] + HINT_ORDER_EPS
                        }
                        last = v
                    }
                }
            }
            sort_part(lnodes, lstart[r], lstart[r + 1], key)
            for i from lstart[r] to lstart[r + 1] {
                pos[lnodes[i]] = i - lstart[r]
            }
        }
        c = count_crossings(nranks, pstart, pitems, psrc, pdst, pos)
        if c < best {
            best = c
            bestpos = copy(pos)
        }
    }
    pos = bestpos
    for r to nranks {
        for i from lstart[r] to lstart[r + 1] {
            key[lnodes[i]] = pos[lnodes[i]]
        }
        sort_part(lnodes, lstart[r], lstart[r + 1], key)
    }
    # transpose (Gansner et al.): two neighbors on a rank change places when
    # that leaves fewer crossings with the ranks on both sides; hinted nodes
    # keep their order
    for sweep to TRANSPOSE_ROUNDS {
        swapped = 0
        for r to nranks {
            for i from lstart[r] to lstart[r + 1] - 1 {
                v = lnodes[i]
                w = lnodes[i + 1]
                if hinting and v < n and w < n and inp.hinted[v] == 1 and inp.hinted[w] == 1 {
                    continue
                }
                keep = pair_crossings(v, w, instart, initems, psrc, outstart, outitems, pdst, pos)
                flip = pair_crossings(w, v, instart, initems, psrc, outstart, outitems, pdst, pos)
                if flip < keep {
                    lnodes[i] = w
                    lnodes[i + 1] = v
                    pos[v] += 1
                    pos[w] -= 1
                    swapped += 1
                }
            }
        }
        if swapped == 0 {
            break
        }
    }
    best = count_crossings(nranks, pstart, pitems, psrc, pdst, pos)

    # ---- coordinates along the ranks: tops of a rank's nodes aligned
    rank_h = zeros(nranks)
    for v to total {
        rank_h[rank[v]] = max(rank_h[rank[v]], nh[v])
    }
    rank_top = zeros(nranks)
    for r from 1 to nranks {
        rank_top[r] = rank_top[r - 1] + rank_h[r - 1] + inp.rank_gap
    }
    y = zeros(total)
    for v to total {
        y[v] = rank_top[rank[v]] + nh[v] / 2
        if v >= n {
            y[v] = rank_top[rank[v]] + rank_h[rank[v]] / 2
        }
    }

    # ---- coordinates across: packed, then pulled toward the neighbors
    x = zeros(total)
    sep = zeros(total)
    for r to nranks {
        at = 0
        for i from lstart[r] to lstart[r + 1] {
            v = lnodes[i]
            if i > lstart[r] {
                at += sep[lnodes[i - 1]]
            }
            x[v] = at
            if i + 1 < lstart[r + 1] {
                u = lnodes[i + 1]
                gap = inp.node_gap
                if v >= n and u >= n {
                    gap = inp.node_gap / 2
                }
                sep[v] = (nw[v] + nw[u]) / 2 + gap
            }
        }
    }
    t = zeros(total)
    wt = zeros(total)
    for sweep to PLACE_SWEEPS {
        down = mod(sweep, 2) == 0
        for step to nranks {
            r = step
            if not down {
                r = nranks - 1 - step
            }
            for i from lstart[r] to lstart[r + 1] {
                v = lnodes[i]
                vals = []
                wts = []
                # the last sweeps listen to both sides
                both = sweep >= PLACE_SWEEPS - 2
                if down or both {
                    for k from instart[v] to instart[v + 1] {
                        p = initems[k]
                        vals = append(vals, x[psrc[p]] + psoff[p] - ptoff[p])
                        wts = append(wts, pweight[p])
                    }
                }
                if (not down) or both {
                    for k from outstart[v] to outstart[v + 1] {
                        p = outitems[k]
                        vals = append(vals, x[pdst[p]] + ptoff[p] - psoff[p])
                        wts = append(wts, pweight[p])
                    }
                }
                # a hinted node outweighs all its edges: it stays where it was
                if v < n and inp.hinted[v] == 1 {
                    vals = append(vals, inp.hint[v])
                    wts = append(wts, sum(wts) + 1)
                }
                if len(vals) == 0 {
                    t[v] = x[v]
                    wt[v] = STAY_WEIGHT
                }
                else {
                    t[v] = weighted_median(vals, wts)
                    wt[v] = sum(wts)
                }
                # when a rank is too crowded for every wish, the dummies give way
                if v < n {
                    wt[v] = wt[v] * REAL_PRIORITY
                }
            }
            place_rank(lnodes, lstart[r], lstart[r + 1], t, wt, sep, x)
        }
    }
    lo = 0
    hi = 0
    for v to total {
        if v == 0 or x[v] - nw[v] / 2 < lo {
            lo = x[v] - nw[v] / 2
        }
        if v == 0 or x[v] + nw[v] / 2 > hi {
            hi = x[v] + nw[v] / 2
        }
    }
    x = x - lo
    width = hi - lo
    height = 0
    if nranks > 0 {
        height = rank_top[nranks - 1] + rank_h[nranks - 1]
    }

    # ---- routes: from the source's bottom through each dummy's rank to the
    # target's top; a long edge whose first (or last) dummy is beside its
    # node leaves (or enters) from the node's side
    route_start = zeros(ne + 1)
    rx = []
    ry = []
    label_x = zeros(ne)
    label_y = zeros(ne)
    for e to ne {
        route_start[e] = len(rx)
        u = inp.efrom[e]
        if a[e] == b[e] {
            # a self loop, on the node's right
            right = x[u] + nw[u] / 2
            px = [right, right + SELF_LOOP_REACH, right + SELF_LOOP_REACH, right]
            py = [y[u] - nh[u] / 4, y[u] - nh[u] / 4, y[u] + nh[u] / 4, y[u] + nh[u] / 4]
            rx = extend(rx, px)
            ry = extend(ry, py)
            label_x[e] = right + SELF_LOOP_REACH + LABEL_PAD + inp.label_w[e] / 2
            label_y[e] = y[u]
            continue
        }
        px = []
        py = []
        first = efirst[e]
        last = efirst[e] + ecount[e] - 1
        src = psrc[first]
        dst = pdst[last]
        # the source's end: from its side when the edge's first lane is
        # beside it and no other node of its rank is in the way
        if ecount[e] > 1 and abs(x[pdst[first]] + doff[pdst[first] - n] - x[src]) > nw[src] / 2 and inp.sides == 1 and clear_beside(src, x[pdst[first]] + doff[pdst[first] - n], n, rank, x, nw) {
            side = 1
            if x[pdst[first]] + doff[pdst[first] - n] < x[src] {
                side = -1
            }
            px = append(px, x[src] + side * nw[src] / 2)
            py = append(py, y[src])
        }
        else {
            px = append(px, x[src] + psoff[first])
            py = append(py, y[src] + nh[src] / 2)
            # a node shorter than its rank: straight down to the rank's foot
            # first, so the edge does not cut across a taller neighbor
            foot = rank_top[rank[src]] + rank_h[rank[src]]
            if foot > y[src] + nh[src] / 2 + KINK / 8 {
                px = append(px, x[src] + psoff[first])
                py = append(py, foot)
            }
        }
        # through each dummy's lane; a lane within KINK of the one before is
        # taken as the same, so a long edge runs straight instead of stepping
        lane = 0
        for p from first to last {
            d = pdst[p]
            lx = x[d] + doff[d - n]
            if p > first and abs(lx - lane) <= KINK {
                lx = lane
            }
            lane = lx
            px = append(px, lx)
            py = append(py, rank_top[rank[d]])
            px = append(px, lx)
            py = append(py, rank_top[rank[d]] + rank_h[rank[d]])
        }
        if ecount[e] > 1 and abs(x[psrc[last]] + doff[psrc[last] - n] - x[dst]) > nw[dst] / 2 and inp.sides == 1 and clear_beside(dst, x[psrc[last]] + doff[psrc[last] - n], n, rank, x, nw) {
            side = 1
            if x[psrc[last]] + doff[psrc[last] - n] < x[dst] {
                side = -1
            }
            px = append(px, x[dst] + side * nw[dst] / 2)
            py = append(py, y[dst])
        }
        else {
            px = append(px, x[dst] + ptoff[last])
            py = append(py, y[dst] - nh[dst] / 2)
        }
        # the label: on its dummy, or beside the middle of a one-rank edge
        if elabel[e] >= 0 {
            label_x[e] = x[elabel[e]] + LABEL_PAD
            label_y[e] = y[elabel[e]]
        }
        else {
            label_x[e] = (px[0] + px[len(px) - 1]) / 2 + LABEL_PAD + inp.label_w[e] / 2
            label_y[e] = (py[0] + py[len(py) - 1]) / 2
        }
        # a point between two on the same vertical line says nothing
        tx = [px[0]]
        ty = [py[0]]
        for i from 1 to len(px) - 1 {
            if not (px[i - 1] == px[i] and px[i] == px[i + 1]) {
                tx = append(tx, px[i])
                ty = append(ty, py[i])
            }
        }
        tx = append(tx, px[len(px) - 1])
        ty = append(ty, py[len(py) - 1])
        px = tx
        py = ty
        # a turned edge's route runs back, from its source to its target
        if rev[e] == 1 {
            px = reversed_copy(px)
            py = reversed_copy(py)
        }
        rx = extend(rx, px)
        ry = extend(ry, py)
    }
    route_start[ne] = len(rx)
    xs = zeros(n)
    ys = zeros(n)
    ranks = zeros(n)
    order = zeros(n)
    for v to n {
        xs[v] = x[v]
        ys[v] = y[v]
        ranks[v] = rank[v]
        order[v] = pos[v]
    }
    return Layered { x: xs, y: ys, rank: ranks, order: order, reversed: rev, route_start: route_start, route_x: rx, route_y: ry, label_x: label_x, label_y: label_y, width: width, height: height, crossings: best }
}

# ---- checks a layout must pass ---------------------------------------------------

#| 1 when no two nodes' boxes overlap.
def no_overlaps(inp: LayoutInput, L: Layered) {
    n = len(inp.w)
    for i to n {
        for j from i + 1 to n {
            dx = abs(L.x[i] - L.x[j]) - (inp.w[i] + inp.w[j]) / 2
            dy = abs(L.y[i] - L.y[j]) - (inp.h[i] + inp.h[j]) / 2
            if dx < 0 and dy < 0 {
                return 0
            }
        }
    }
    return 1
}

#| 1 when every edge has a route of at least two points, starting on its
#| source's box and ending on its target's.
def every_edge_drawn(inp: LayoutInput, L: Layered) {
    ne = len(inp.efrom)
    for e to ne {
        lo = L.route_start[e]
        hi = L.route_start[e + 1]
        if hi - lo < 2 {
            return 0
        }
        if not on_box(L.route_x[lo], L.route_y[lo], L.x[inp.efrom[e]], L.y[inp.efrom[e]], inp.w[inp.efrom[e]], inp.h[inp.efrom[e]]) {
            return 0
        }
        if not on_box(L.route_x[hi - 1], L.route_y[hi - 1], L.x[inp.eto[e]], L.y[inp.eto[e]], inp.w[inp.eto[e]], inp.h[inp.eto[e]]) {
            return 0
        }
    }
    return 1
}

#| Whether (px, py) is on the border of the box centered on (x, y), to a
#| hundredth.
def on_box(px, py, x, y, w, h) {
    tol = 0.01
    inside = abs(px - x) <= w / 2 + tol and abs(py - y) <= h / 2 + tol
    border = abs(abs(px - x) - w / 2) <= tol or abs(abs(py - y) - h / 2) <= tol
    return inside and border
}

#| 1 when every edge not turned around goes to a later rank, and every
#| turned one to an earlier rank (self loops aside).
def ranks_follow_edges(inp: LayoutInput, L: Layered) {
    for e to len(inp.efrom) {
        u = inp.efrom[e]
        v = inp.eto[e]
        if u == v {
            continue
        }
        if L.reversed[e] == 0 and L.rank[v] <= L.rank[u] {
            return 0
        }
        if L.reversed[e] == 1 and L.rank[v] >= L.rank[u] {
            return 0
        }
    }
    return 1
}

#| 1 when the two layouts are the same, number for number.
def same_layout(A: Layered, B: Layered) {
    same = len(A.x) == len(B.x) and len(A.route_x) == len(B.route_x)
    if not same {
        return 0
    }
    if not (all(A.x == B.x) and all(A.y == B.y) and all(A.route_x == B.route_x) and all(A.route_y == B.route_y)) {
        return 0
    }
    return 1
}

#| Every invariant at once.
def layout_ok(inp: LayoutInput, L: Layered) {
    return no_overlaps(inp, L) == 1 and every_edge_drawn(inp, L) == 1 and ranks_follow_edges(inp, L) == 1
}

test "a chain is one node per rank, in a straight line" {
    inp = layout_input([40, 40, 40], [20, 20, 20], [0, 1], [1, 2], 10, 20)
    L = layered(inp)
    assert_true(all(L.rank == [0, 1, 2]))
    assert_near(L.x[0], L.x[2], 1e-9)
    assert_near(L.y[1] - L.y[0], 40, 1e-9)
    assert_true(layout_ok(inp, L))
}

test "a diamond has no crossings and a symmetric middle" {
    inp = layout_input([30, 30, 30, 30], [20, 20, 20, 20], [0, 0, 1, 2], [1, 2, 3, 3], 10, 20)
    L = layered(inp)
    assert_true(L.crossings == 0)
    assert_true(L.rank[3] == 2)
    assert_near(L.x[0], L.x[3], 1e-9)
    assert_near(L.x[0] - L.x[1], L.x[2] - L.x[0], 1e-9)
    assert_true(layout_ok(inp, L))
}

test "the sweeps uncross K2,2, which the input order draws crossed" {
    # 0 -> 3, 1 -> 2: in index order the two edges cross; the sweeps uncross them
    inp = layout_input([30, 30, 30, 30], [20, 20, 20, 20], [0, 1], [3, 2], 10, 20)
    L = layered(inp)
    assert_true(L.crossings == 0)
    assert_true(layout_ok(inp, L))
}

test "a cycle is broken, and a back edge marked by the caller stays back" {
    inp = layout_input([30, 30, 30], [20, 20, 20], [0, 1, 2], [1, 2, 0], 10, 20)
    L = layered(inp)
    assert_true(sum(L.reversed) == 1)
    assert_true(L.reversed[2] == 1)
    assert_true(layout_ok(inp, L))
    # a loop's carried value: step 2 feeds step 0 on the next pass
    inp2 = layout_input([30, 30, 30], [20, 20, 20], [0, 1, 2], [1, 2, 0], 10, 20)
    inp2.eback[2] = 1
    L2 = layered(inp2)
    assert_true(all(L2.reversed == [0, 0, 1]))
    assert_true(all(L2.rank == [0, 1, 2]))
    # its route starts on step 2 and ends on step 0
    lo = L2.route_start[2]
    hi = L2.route_start[3]
    assert_near(L2.route_y[lo], L2.y[2], 10)
    assert_near(L2.route_y[hi - 1], L2.y[0], 10)
    assert_true(layout_ok(inp2, L2))
}

test "a long edge goes around, through dummies, and its label has room" {
    # 0 -> 1 -> 2 -> 3 and 0 -> 3 labeled
    inp = layout_input([60, 60, 60, 60], [20, 20, 20, 20], [0, 1, 2, 0], [1, 2, 3, 3], 10, 20)
    inp.label_w[3] = 50
    inp.label_h[3] = 12
    L = layered(inp)
    lo = L.route_start[3]
    hi = L.route_start[4]
    # two dummies in one straight lane: the two ends and the lane's two ends
    assert_true(hi - lo == 4)
    # the chain stays straight (to a unit), and the label, beside node 2, is clear of it
    straight = 1
    assert_near(L.x[0], L.x[3], straight)
    assert_near(L.x[1], L.x[2], straight)
    assert_true(abs(L.label_x[3] - L.x[2]) >= (60 + 50) / 2)
    # the label's text starts right of the line
    lane_x = L.route_x[lo + 3]
    assert_true(L.label_x[3] - 50 / 2 >= lane_x)
    assert_true(layout_ok(inp, L))
}

test "a self loop is drawn on its node" {
    inp = layout_input([30, 30], [20, 20], [0, 1], [1, 1], 10, 20)
    L = layered(inp)
    assert_true(L.route_start[2] - L.route_start[1] == 4)
    assert_true(layout_ok(inp, L))
}

test "nodes of different sizes do not overlap, and the output is the same twice" {
    w = [120, 30, 80, 30, 200, 50, 40]
    h = [60, 20, 90, 20, 30, 20, 20]
    efrom = [0, 0, 0, 1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 5, 1]
    eto = [1, 2, 3, 4, 4, 5, 6, 6, 6, 6]
    inp = layout_input(w, h, efrom, eto, 12, 24)
    L = layered(inp)
    assert_true(layout_ok(inp, L))
    assert_true(same_layout(L, layered(inp)) == 1)
}

test "ports pull the target toward the side the edge leaves from" {
    # node 0 is wide and calls 1 from its left part and 2 from its right part
    inp = layout_input([200, 40, 40], [40, 20, 20], [0, 0], [2, 1], 10, 20)
    inp.sport[0] = 80
    inp.sport[1] = -80
    L = layered(inp)
    assert_true(L.x[1] < L.x[2])
    assert_true(layout_ok(inp, L))
}

test "an edge that must span two ranks leaves one empty between" {
    inp = layout_input([30, 30, 30], [20, 20, 20], [0, 1], [1, 2], 10, 20)
    inp.elen[0] = 2
    L = layered(inp)
    assert_true(all(L.rank == [0, 2, 3]))
    assert_true(layout_ok(inp, L))
}

test "hints keep an earlier layout's nodes where they were" {
    # 0 -> 1, 0 -> 2, 1 -> 3; then a new node 4 under 2, hinted with the first layout
    inp = layout_input([40, 40, 40, 40], [20, 20, 20, 20], [0, 0, 1], [1, 2, 3], 10, 20)
    L = layered(inp)
    grown = layout_input([40, 40, 40, 40, 40], [20, 20, 20, 20, 20], [0, 0, 1, 2], [1, 2, 3, 4], 10, 20)
    hint = [L.x[0], L.x[1], L.x[2], L.x[3], 0]
    L2 = layered(LayoutInput { hint: hint, hinted: [1, 1, 1, 1, 0], ..grown })
    for k to 4 {
        assert_near(L2.x[k] - L2.x[0], L.x[k] - L.x[0], 1e-9)
    }
    assert_near(L2.x[4], L2.x[2], 1e-9)
    assert_true(layout_ok(grown, L2))
    # a hint that puts 2 left of 1 is kept, though the sweeps would not care
    swapped = [L.x[0], L.x[2], L.x[1], L.x[2], 0]
    L3 = layered(LayoutInput { hint: swapped, hinted: [1, 1, 1, 0, 0], ..grown })
    assert_true(L3.x[2] < L3.x[1])
    assert_true(layout_ok(grown, L3))
}

test "an edge from a node shorter than its rank drops to the rank's foot first" {
    # 0 is short beside the tall 1; 0 -> 2 leaves 0 straight down past 1's height
    inp = layout_input([40, 40, 40], [10, 60, 10], [0, 1], [2, 2], 10, 20)
    L = layered(inp)
    lo = L.route_start[0]
    assert_near(L.route_x[lo + 1], L.route_x[lo], 1e-9)
    assert_near(L.route_y[lo + 1], 60, 1e-9)
    assert_true(layout_ok(inp, L))
}

